<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Cms on jpcercal.com</title><link>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/tags/cms/</link><description>Recent content in Cms on jpcercal.com</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 22 Oct 2013 12:05:38 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/tags/cms/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>WordPress Tip: How to use Shortcodes</title><link>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/wordpress-tip-how-to-use-shortcodes/</link><pubDate>Tue, 22 Oct 2013 12:05:38 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/wordpress-tip-how-to-use-shortcodes/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Since version &lt;em&gt;2.5+&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;WordPress&lt;/em&gt; has had a feature known as &lt;em&gt;shortcodes&lt;/em&gt;, it works similarly to&#10;filters, because they accept parameters (attributes) and return a result.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Well, shortcodes are extremely useful and easy to use, allowing developers to create&#10;custom content for users to add to their pages.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Next we&amp;rsquo;ll see how simple it is to add a shortcode to your theme. So we&amp;rsquo;ll get to know the&#10;&lt;code&gt;do_shortcode()&lt;/code&gt; function.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To use this function, just add the following code to your theme:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>WordPress Tip: How to check whether a plugin is active?</title><link>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/wordpress-tip-how-to-check-whether-a-plugin-is-active/</link><pubDate>Wed, 28 Aug 2013 17:40:54 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/wordpress-tip-how-to-check-whether-a-plugin-is-active/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;When you&amp;rsquo;re developing a theme or a &lt;em&gt;plugin&lt;/em&gt; for the &lt;em&gt;WordPress&lt;/em&gt; platform, you may need to check&#10;whether a specific &lt;em&gt;plugin&lt;/em&gt; is activated. Well, here&amp;rsquo;s a simple &lt;em&gt;script&lt;/em&gt; to check whether a &lt;em&gt;plugin&lt;/em&gt;&#10;is activated or not in the &lt;em&gt;wordpress&lt;/em&gt; administration panel.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You&amp;rsquo;ll only need to change line 4 to your &lt;em&gt;plugin&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/em&gt; directory name.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Plugins&lt;/em&gt; are located in the directory: &lt;code&gt;/wp-content/plugins/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 3&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 4&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 5&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 6&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 7&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 8&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 9&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;10&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;11&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;12&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-php" data-lang="php"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;php&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Adicione esta linha se este pedaço de código&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// não estiver sendo executado no painel administrativo&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;require_once&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ABSPATH&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;/wp-admin/includes/plugin.php&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Verifica se o plugin está ativado...&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;is_plugin_active&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;plugin-directory/plugin-file.php&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// o plugin está ativado...&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// O plugin está desativado...&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;That was another tip for the &lt;em&gt;WordPress&lt;/em&gt; platform.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>WordPress Hack: How to get a Post's content by ID</title><link>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/wordpress-hack-how-to-get-a-posts-content-by-id/</link><pubDate>Fri, 23 Aug 2013 14:52:26 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/wordpress-hack-how-to-get-a-posts-content-by-id/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;When you&amp;rsquo;re building a theme for WordPress, you may need to get the content of a specific post&#10;using the &lt;strong&gt;ID&lt;/strong&gt; as a filter. Most of the time you get a post&amp;rsquo;s content through the &lt;em&gt;get_post_content&lt;/em&gt; function&#10;inside a &lt;em&gt;Loop&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;However, when you need to retrieve a post&amp;rsquo;s information outside the &lt;em&gt;loop&lt;/em&gt; context or at a separate point&#10;in the application, the best solution is to use the &lt;code&gt;get_post_field('field-name'), $postId)&lt;/code&gt; function.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>How to get a Page Permalink</title><link>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/how-to-get-a-page-permalink/</link><pubDate>Sat, 09 Feb 2013 10:17:18 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/how-to-get-a-page-permalink/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Today we needed to get the &lt;strong&gt;permalink&lt;/strong&gt; of a page in &lt;em&gt;WordPress&lt;/em&gt; whose &lt;em&gt;post_type&lt;/em&gt; is &amp;ldquo;&lt;em&gt;page&lt;/em&gt;&amp;rdquo;. To do this, we had to&#10;combine two functions, which are: &lt;code&gt;get_permalink()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;get_page_by_path()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to Get a Page Permalink using the Page Name:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-php" data-lang="php"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;lt;?php echo get_permalink( get_page_by_path(&amp;#39;Eventos&amp;#39;) ); ?&amp;gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;php&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;_e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;Eventos&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;jpcercal.com&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cp"&gt;?&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to Get a Page Permalink using the Page Slug:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-php" data-lang="php"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;lt;?php echo get_permalink( get_page_by_path(&amp;#39;cadastrar-cliente&amp;#39;) ); ?&amp;gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;php&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;_e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;Cadastrar Cliente&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;jpcercal.com&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cp"&gt;?&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;lt;/a&amp;gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note About Page Hierarchy and Slugs.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Inserting users in WordPress with wp_insert_user</title><link>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/inserting-users-in-wordpress-with-wp_insert_user/</link><pubDate>Thu, 24 Jan 2013 10:16:39 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/inserting-users-in-wordpress-with-wp_insert_user/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The wp_insert_user function inserts a user into the WordPress database. It can also update a user&#10;if the ID key is present in the array passed to the function as a parameter.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 3&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 4&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 5&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 6&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 7&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 8&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 9&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;10&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;11&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-php" data-lang="php"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;php&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt;/**&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt; * Insere um usuário na base de dados do WordPress&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt; *&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt; * @param $userdata mixed Um array com os dados do usuário, stdClass ou um objeto WP_User&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt; *&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt; * @return mixed Se sucesso, retorna o ID do usuário que acaba de ser criado,&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt; * do contrário retorna um objeto WP_Error&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt; */&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;wp_insert_user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$userdata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;$userdata&lt;/code&gt; array should contain the following fields:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Excerpts on WordPress 3.0+ pages</title><link>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/excerpts-on-wordpress-3-0-pages/</link><pubDate>Sun, 09 Dec 2012 03:12:27 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/excerpts-on-wordpress-3-0-pages/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;ve ever needed to add excerpts to pages in WordPress 3.0+, you can be happy because the tip is&#10;very simple. Just add the following code to a file that wordpress loads automatically.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;3&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;4&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;5&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;6&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-php" data-lang="php"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;php&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt;/**&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt; * @param string $post_type&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt; * @param string|array $supports&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="sd"&gt; */&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;add_post_type_support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;search&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;excerpt&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Usually the code above is placed in an &amp;ldquo;init&amp;rdquo; &lt;em&gt;action hook&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This will enable a new field in the administration panel, letting you add an &lt;strong&gt;excerpt&lt;/strong&gt; to your&#10;&lt;strong&gt;pages&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Custom Fields in the Joomla panel</title><link>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/custom-fields-in-the-joomla-panel/</link><pubDate>Mon, 10 Oct 2011 17:32:40 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://staging.jpcercal.com/pr-143/en/custom-fields-in-the-joomla-panel/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Hello, today I needed to add a custom field to the&#10;&lt;a href="http://www.joomla.org/" title="Joomla"&gt;Joomla&lt;/a&gt; 1.6 administration panel for a component I was developing, and decided to share&#10;the &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;recipe&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt; here on my blog.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This tutorial was developed based on the&#10;&lt;a href="http://docs.joomla.org/Creating_a_custom_form_field_type" title="Official Joomla Documentation"&gt;Official Joomla Documentation&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To create a &lt;strong&gt;custom field&lt;/strong&gt; type for &lt;em&gt;Joomla 1.6&lt;/em&gt;, you must create a class that extends a field type&#10;already defined by &lt;em&gt;Joomla&lt;/em&gt; itself (&lt;em&gt;media&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;text&lt;/em&gt;, etc), or else the base class for this functionality,&#10;which is &lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;JFormField&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>